<p>
    Studying Applied Informatics has given me insights into the technology field that I never had before. 
Before starting my studies, I thought informatics was mostly about coding and building software. 
However, I quickly discovered that the field is much larger and more diverse than most outsiders imagine.
From algorithms and databases to cybersecurity, networking, artificial intelligence, and project management, Applied Informatics covers a wide range of disciplines. Looking back, there are many things I wish I had known before starting this journey. 
They would not have changed my decision, but they would have helped me prepare better for what was ahead.
</p>

